From: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: wcss: copy coredump before recovery

The secure WCSS PIL driver selects inline coredumps. The remoteproc core
waits for an inline dump to be consumed, or for devcoredump's five minute
timeout, before it reloads the crashed remote processor. This leaves every
ath12k device in the WSI group unavailable long after q6wcss crashes.

Use the copied coredump mode instead. It snapshots the WCSS regions while
the remote processor is stopped, then allows recovery to continue without
depending on a userspace dump reader.

Also copy the final chunk before releasing its temporary mapping. A full
segment copy has offset plus size equal to the segment size, so the old
condition unmapped the segment without copying any data. This ordering
matches Qualcomm's downstream secure WCSS driver.

This follows the recovery lifecycle of the upstream remoteproc core while
retaining the dump regions added by the secure PIL driver.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260713-rproc-v13-3-41011cbcda3e@oss.qualcomm.com
Link: https://github.com/Telecominfraproject/wlan-ap/blob/4dda11dcf7455828e03a753079c520701f2f7a7c/feeds/qca-wifi-7/ipq53xx/files-6.6/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c
Signed-off-by: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_wcss_sec.c
@@ -137,9 +137,9 @@ static void wcss_sec_copy_segment(struct
 		return;
 }
 
-	if (offset + size < segment->size) {
-		memcpy(dest, segment->io_ptr + offset, size);
-	} else {
+	memcpy(dest, segment->io_ptr + offset, size);
+
+	if (offset + size >= segment->size) {
 		iounmap(segment->io_ptr);
 		segment->io_ptr = NULL;
 }
@@ -271,7 +272,7 @@ static int wcss_sec_probe(struct platform
 }
 
 	rproc->auto_boot = false;
-	rproc->dump_conf = RPROC_COREDUMP_INLINE;
+	rproc->dump_conf = RPROC_COREDUMP_ENABLED;
 	rproc_coredump_set_elf_info(rproc, ELFCLASS32, EM_NONE);
 
 	ret = devm_rproc_add(&pdev->dev, rproc);
